facts:
**Line:** $y=mx+c$, or a rearrangement like $x+2y=6$, has $x$ and $y$ to the power $1$ and a straight graph.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->] (-2.8,-1.7)--(2.8,2.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Parabola:** $y=ax^{2}+bx+c$ has highest power $2$ in $x$ only, giving a U-shape opening up when $a>0$ and down when $a<0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-1.2:2.2,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x-0.5)*(\x-0.5)-1.5});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Exponential:** $y=a^{x}$ has $x$ as the **exponent**, so the curve gets steeper and steeper, falls instead for $a^{-x}$, and has a horizontal asymptote.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-3:1.55,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.85*exp(\x*ln(2))});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Hyperbola:** $y=\dfrac{k}{x}$, or equivalently $xy=k$, has $x$ in the **denominator**, and its graph is two separate branches with two asymptotes.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=0.42:3,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.3/\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-3:-0.42,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.3/\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Circle:** $x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}$, or $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}=r^{2}$ with centre $(a,b)$, squares and adds **both** $x$ and $y$, and its graph is a closed round curve.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (2);
\fill (0,0) circle (0.07);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.414,1.414) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Cubic:** $y=x^{3}$ has highest power $3$, with a central point where the curve flattens and then keeps rising.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-1.45:1.45,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

